Re-vendors the estate hooks from rarebit-one/agent-estate@4eb9d7b with `estate-sync --estate`. `estate-sync --check` is clean afterwards.

The main change is the pre-push-prepare resolver fixes from rarebit-one/agent-estate#33 (which closes agent-estate#23):
- inside `"…"`, `${…}` now nests, so its inner quotes stay data (P1: the hook could resolve the wrong checkout);
- `.` counts as the source builtin only in command position, so `git add . && git push` no longer skips the hook;
- `--force-with-lease` goes on the lexed push segment, not on the first textual match;
- a HOME change before a bare `cd` or `~` makes the target unknown;
- comments inside `$( … )`, redirections or assignment prefixes before `.`, and UTF-8 byte offsets in the lease placement.

Files: `.agents/estate.lock .agents/hooks/enforce-worktree-bash.sh .agents/hooks/pre-push-prepare.sh `. These are vendored, hash-locked copies of canonical code that was reviewed in agent-estate#33.

